## 1. What's changing and why

The weekend peek left one open defect: the hand-mirrored seam B recomposition (`asr`, `F0`, `N`, `style` → decoder → audio) is not parity-clean against the full-model reference (maxdiff ~0.075 on the waveform). Prime suspect is the `strict=False` state-dict load silently dropping or mismatching decoder weight keys. Until that is isolated and fixed, no ONNX export happens — exporting a wrong decoder would poison every downstream measurement.

Sequence (unchanged from note_16, now gated):

```text
G0 strict-load  →  G1 recomposition parity (hook ladder)
      →  G2 decoder-only ONNX @ fixed T (ORT parity + ears)
      →  G3 OV-GPU static matrix (cold/warm/restart/CACHE_DIR)  →  GO / KILL
```

Each gate is a hard precondition for the next. No gate may be relaxed after its measurement exists; changes to a gate require a Nexus call recorded in the notes.

